Attribute Meaning <code>type</code> Required by the Tala XML compiler. Supported question types are <code>goal</code>, <code>wh_question</code>, <code>kpq</code>, <code>alt_question</code>, and <code>yn_question</code>. <code>predicate</code> Predicate for a predicate-backed question. <code>insist</code> Optional Boolean. When true, reopens the issue even if it was already resolved. <p>Without insistence, an issue already resolved in shared commitments does not need to be raised again. With <code>insist="true"</code>, existing resolving answers are cleared and the question is raised again.</p> <p>Question content can include <code>embedded_question</code> for a KPQ. A KPQ wraps the question whose answer is being checked:</p> <pre><code>&lt;assume_issue type="kpq"&gt;
  &lt;embedded_question type="wh_question" predicate="destination"/&gt;
&lt;/assume_issue&gt;
</code></pre>

Attribute Meaning <code>expected_passivity</code> Required decimal duration in seconds for the client to wait for further user input. <p>The element has no children and can appear in a plan or a conditional branch. The explicit value does not change passivity timing for turns handed over by the normal dialogue flow. It requests a handoff at this point; it does not guarantee that all output in the turn is caused by this particular plan item.</p> <pre><code>&lt;plan&gt;
  &lt;inform&gt;
    &lt;proposition predicate="instructions" value="Follow the next steps."/&gt;
  &lt;/inform&gt;
  &lt;end_turn expected_passivity="3.0"/&gt;
&lt;/plan&gt;
</code></pre>
